# Committed deliberately, as belt and braces.
#
# The same patterns are in .git/info/exclude, which is LOCAL ONLY and does not
# survive a re-clone — the same weakness as the merge driver and the pre-commit
# hook (see docs/local-workflow.md). For those two a fresh clone loses a safety
# net. For this one it loses nothing until the first `git add .`, which would
# then commit a bytecode cache.
#
# That is a live risk rather than a theoretical one: watchlist.py is the one
# script this repo explicitly encourages running locally, and every run creates
# __pycache__/.

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Claude Code SESSION files. Agents and skills are project configuration
# rather than session state — they are the loop's gate and driver, and a
# re-clone without them cannot run it — so they are negated back in.
# NOT `.claude/`. Git never descends into an excluded DIRECTORY, so a negation
# inside one can never re-include anything — `!.claude/agents/` under
# `.claude/` silently does nothing, and the files just never get committed.
# Excluding the CONTENTS instead leaves the directory walkable so the
# negations bite. Verified with `git check-ignore -v`, not by reading the man
# page.
.claude/*
!.claude/agents/
!.claude/skills/

# SDD scratch: ledgers, briefs, review packages. Regenerable, and the git
# history is the real record once a plan is done.
.superpowers/

# Local virtualenvs. Nothing here needs one, but the local-run instructions
# invite creating one, and a committed venv is 15MB of someone else's platform.
venv/
.venv/
